      "id": "0c2e0a94058f51eca9186dca817c93c30d0e4ef9",
      "message": "confirm the OTA-1718 iPhone 14 profile against the reporting device\n\nThe tester caught the edge of the covered SEND button and a log went. It carries\nthe device's own metrics \u2014 window 390x844, ios 26.4.2, on OTA-1716 \u2014 so the\nwindow height the layout arithmetic reasons about is now the number the phone\nreported rather than one read off a spec page.\n\nThe same log carries the report's DESCRIPTION field, and it is three characters:\n\"log\". That is the defect writing its own summary. She could reach the field and\ncould not reach SEND well enough to have written anything into it first.\n\nTest-only; no behaviour change and no stamp.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
